    "body": "TODO: let me review it\r\n\r\nThe GEMM-swizzled path of quantize_contiguous_kernel gathered each 16-byte scale run through warp shuffles and shared memory, then flushed it after a CTA barrier. Store each scale byte directly at its swizzled index instead, as the packed path does. Outputs are bit-identical; swizzled bf16 rowwise quantization is ~2.4% faster on average (up to ~5.5%) on GB200.\r\n\r\n# Description\r\n\r\nPlease include a brief summary of the changes, relevant motivation and context.\r\n\r\nBenchmark: https://claude.ai/artifact/VpCXcAtAvbCe7gfxWBEwLV?sk=XE0XRwAptECOploI4sXZeA\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [ ] Documentation change (change only to the documentation, either a fix or a new content)\r\n- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n- [ ] Infra/Build change\r\n- [ ] Code refactoring\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\nPlease list the changes introduced in this PR:\r\n\r\n- Change A\r\n- Change B\r\n\r\n# Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [ ] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\r\n- [ ] The functionality is complete\r\n- [ ] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\r\n- [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\r\n- [ ] My changes generate no new warnings\r\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\r\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\r\n",
